statement:
Fix a prime $p$, and let $P_1,\dots,P_{\mathrm{width}}$ be polynomials in the variables $y_1,\dots,y_{\mathrm{vars}}$ over $\bbz/p$, together with subsets $S_1,\dots,S_\ell$ of the index set $\{1,\dots,\mathrm{width}\}$. Then for every point $y : \{1,\dots,\mathrm{vars}\} \to \bbz/p$, evaluating the randomized OR-approximating polynomial $1 - \prod_{k=1}^{\ell}\bigl(1 - (\sum_{i \in S_k} P_i)^{p-1}\bigr)$ at $y$ yields the value obtained by feeding the scalars $P_1(y),\dots,P_{\mathrm{width}}(y)$ into the value-level OR approximator with the same subsets:
\[
\Bigl(1 - \prod_{k=1}^{\ell}\bigl(1 - (\textstyle\sum_{i \in S_k} P_i)^{p-1}\bigr)\Bigr)\!\big|_{y}
\;=\;
1 - \prod_{k=1}^{\ell}\Bigl(1 - \bigl(\textstyle\sum_{i \in S_k} P_i(y)\bigr)^{p-1}\Bigr).
\]
